1
00:00:05,801 --> 00:00:07,411
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,436 --> 00:00:09,097
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:24,507 --> 00:00:26,129
I don't want to wake up.

4
00:00:56,151 --> 00:00:57,366
Did you sleep well?

5
00:00:59,666 --> 00:01:04,017
I saw you in my dream again,
and I wanted to stay asleep so badly.

6
00:01:05,513 --> 00:01:08,228
I keep trying not to be happy just yet,

7
00:01:08,955 --> 00:01:11,395
but today, I just want to be happy.

8
00:01:12,467 --> 00:01:14,678
Have a great day, Mu Jin.

9
00:01:36,573 --> 00:01:38,673
(Episode 23)

10
00:01:40,325 --> 00:01:41,473
What?

11
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:47,413
Just hit me. I deserve a beating.

12
00:01:48,547 --> 00:01:49,954
What did you do to deserve a beating?

13
00:01:51,047 --> 00:01:53,204
Just hit me. Hit me first, then listen.

14
00:01:54,547 --> 00:01:56,264
What am I, a gangster?

15
00:02:00,827 --> 00:02:02,002
You know this, right?

16
00:02:02,032 --> 00:02:04,732
It's the coat your father left you.

17
00:02:05,567 --> 00:02:06,833
Why do you have this?

18
00:02:07,487 --> 00:02:10,674
Last night I went on a date
with the woman I met on a blind date,

19
00:02:10,699 --> 00:02:13,035
and I had nothing decent to wear,
so I wore your coat.

20
00:02:13,073 --> 00:02:15,380
- Okay.
- But on a park bench...

21
00:02:16,094 --> 00:02:18,884
I didn't know it had just been painted,
and I plopped right down on it.

22
00:02:22,577 --> 00:02:24,622
Hey, are you out of your mind?

23
00:02:24,647 --> 00:02:27,142
Do you know what this coat means to me?

24
00:02:27,167 --> 00:02:29,766
That's why I said I deserve a beating.

25
00:02:29,791 --> 00:02:32,382
Hit me. Hit me until you feel better.

26
00:02:45,074 --> 00:02:46,345
You're not going to hit me?

27
00:02:48,534 --> 00:02:49,680
You're smiling?

28
00:02:50,027 --> 00:02:53,104
Today, I'll forgive you
no matter what you do.

29
00:02:53,129 --> 00:02:54,693
Why? How come?

30
00:02:55,733 --> 00:02:58,613
So you can hit me with a hammer
when I let my guard down.

31
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:03,395
No, let's just call it
a Liberation Day pardon.

32
00:03:03,667 --> 00:03:06,433
What, did you win back
some lost territory?

33
00:03:06,733 --> 00:03:09,893
I found my lost Gyu Rim.

34
00:03:12,507 --> 00:03:16,064
You're alive today all thanks to Gyu Rim.

35
00:03:16,345 --> 00:03:18,438
Thank her later.

36
00:03:24,332 --> 00:03:25,702
Thank you, Rim.

37
00:03:33,787 --> 00:03:36,065
Gyeol, let's eat.

38
00:03:40,046 --> 00:03:43,473
Looks good. Thanks for the food.

39
00:03:44,866 --> 00:03:47,955
Gyeol, listen to me while you eat.

40
00:03:50,773 --> 00:03:54,858
I'm going to give it my all
with Mu Jin from now on.

41
00:03:54,967 --> 00:03:58,672
I won't avoid him anymore
or do anything weird,

42
00:03:58,806 --> 00:04:01,912
and I'm going to give it everything
I've got. For real.

43
00:04:05,859 --> 00:04:07,653
Good decision.

44
00:04:07,953 --> 00:04:12,083
I promise you, Gyeol,
I'm going to do my very best,

45
00:04:15,413 --> 00:04:19,009
but I don't think love
always has to end in marriage.

46
00:04:19,053 --> 00:04:23,064
Why? People get married
because they're in love.

47
00:04:23,666 --> 00:04:26,866
You can get married without being in love,

48
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:29,807
and you can be in love
and still not get married.

49
00:04:30,647 --> 00:04:35,295
So even if Mu Jin and I
don't end up getting married,

50
00:04:35,409 --> 00:04:39,315
try not to be too disappointed,
and try to understand, okay?

51
00:04:41,466 --> 00:04:45,639
I served this bean sprout soup earlier
when it was piping hot. How is it now?

52
00:04:45,799 --> 00:04:47,812
It's probably cooled down a lot.
Want to try?

53
00:04:52,026 --> 00:04:53,967
Yeah, it's really cooled down.

54
00:04:55,105 --> 00:04:56,826
Feelings are like that too.

55
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:59,654
Even if you're crazy about someone now,

56
00:04:59,814 --> 00:05:03,534
over time, feelings can cool down
like this bean sprout soup.

57
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:07,501
Mu Jin's feelings might cool,
or mine might.

58
00:05:07,653 --> 00:05:11,243
Then you can just heat it up
in the microwave.

59
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:16,092
Some things can't be heated up
in the microwave again.

60
00:05:16,187 --> 00:05:18,587
Feelings don't work that way.

61
00:05:19,745 --> 00:05:23,963
Like how I can't like my grandpa
no matter how hard I try?

62
00:05:25,612 --> 00:05:27,432
Well, that's...

63
00:05:27,871 --> 00:05:33,065
I guess I can't say
that's a bad comparison.

64
00:05:34,059 --> 00:05:35,746
I know what you mean.

65
00:05:36,613 --> 00:05:39,007
I'm trying not to,

66
00:05:39,473 --> 00:05:43,427
but my feelings for my grandpa
won't warm back up.

67
00:05:43,946 --> 00:05:50,644
Gyu Seo said his heart turns to ice
whenever he sees my grandpa.

68
00:05:53,206 --> 00:05:56,876
Seriously, what kind of father are you?

69
00:05:57,034 --> 00:05:59,906
What did I do?

70
00:06:01,465 --> 00:06:03,984
What kind of amazing romance
are you having...

71
00:06:04,185 --> 00:06:07,078
that you steal Gyu O's clothes
and even his cologne?

72
00:06:07,587 --> 00:06:09,447
You never even bought him a pair of socks.

73
00:06:09,547 --> 00:06:13,677
Did you see whether or not
I ever bought Gyu O socks?

74
00:06:13,787 --> 00:06:17,437
When I was making good money,
I even had suits made for your brother.

75
00:06:17,507 --> 00:06:19,967
Han Gyu O was the prince
of Pyeongchang-dong.

76
00:06:20,133 --> 00:06:23,482
If only your mom hadn't had an affair
and run off with all my money.

77
00:06:23,507 --> 00:06:27,631
Exactly. Why did you ever bring
a woman like that home?

78
00:06:28,173 --> 00:06:30,579
Why did you kick out Gyu Rim's mom,
such a good woman,

79
00:06:30,623 --> 00:06:32,239
and bring in that con artist instead?

80
00:06:32,312 --> 00:06:34,515
She said she was pregnant with you.
What was I supposed to do?

81
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:38,394
She threatened to get rid of you
unless I married her. What could I do?

82
00:06:38,447 --> 00:06:40,603
You should've just let her get rid of us.

83
00:06:40,813 --> 00:06:42,853
Then Gyu Min and I
would never have been born. Great.

84
00:06:42,878 --> 00:06:45,473
How can you say that to me,
you little punk?

85
00:06:45,538 --> 00:06:48,590
Where's something to hit you with?
You little punk.

86
00:06:49,169 --> 00:06:55,489
Gyu Rim, Gyu Seo's asking me
why I had him and Gyu Min.

87
00:06:55,514 --> 00:06:58,376
He's driving a nail into my heart again.

88
00:07:01,133 --> 00:07:04,525
I told you not to say things like that,
didn't I?

89
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:07,661
I told you I wouldn't let it slide
if you said that one more time, didn't I?

90
00:07:08,222 --> 00:07:09,898
Even if you gave me the whole world,

91
00:07:10,187 --> 00:07:11,987
I'd never trade you and Gyu Min.

92
00:07:13,127 --> 00:07:17,376
Who are you to talk like that
about my precious siblings?

93
00:07:17,567 --> 00:07:20,409
Do you really want to get in big trouble
with me? Seriously?

94
00:07:29,011 --> 00:07:34,580
That kid sucks up to the strong
and stomps on the weak.

95
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:39,044
You can't say a word
when your sister scolds you,

96
00:07:39,069 --> 00:07:42,031
but you yell at and threaten
your own weak old father.

97
00:07:42,056 --> 00:07:43,349
That kid...

98
00:07:43,648 --> 00:07:47,890
What are you going to do when I'm dead
and there's no one left to pick on?

99
00:07:48,307 --> 00:07:50,483
You didn't do anything right either, Dad.

100
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:54,619
I never once said I did anything right.

101
00:07:54,947 --> 00:07:56,867
I'm just saying I had no choice.

102
00:07:57,047 --> 00:08:00,301
I was so charming
that women wouldn't leave me alone,

103
00:08:00,332 --> 00:08:02,112
and there was no way I could stop them.

104
00:08:02,137 --> 00:08:04,803
Why did you say something so pointless
in front of Gyeol?

105
00:08:05,759 --> 00:08:07,990
What did I say to Gyeol?

106
00:08:08,346 --> 00:08:10,744
Why is Gyeol a burden?

107
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:15,487
Why would you say that in front of him
and break my baby's heart?

108
00:08:15,793 --> 00:08:19,494
No, I...

109
00:08:19,827 --> 00:08:21,807
Gyeol heard that?

110
00:08:23,813 --> 00:08:29,065
If I had to choose between Gyeol and you,
I'd choose Gyeol in a heartbeat.

111
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:33,235
Are you serious?
I'm your own flesh and blood.

112
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:37,098
Gyeol is my son too. I gave birth to him.

113
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:42,804
He was born from my heart.
He's the most precious thing in my world.

114
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:47,448
I'm just saying,
blood is thicker than water,

115
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:50,026
so my kid matters more to me than yours.

116
00:08:50,113 --> 00:08:55,357
When my kid cries, I cry tears of blood.

117
00:08:56,295 --> 00:08:57,800
Why don't you get that?

118
00:09:05,716 --> 00:09:10,433
So that little kid Gyeol heard it?

119
00:09:12,433 --> 00:09:17,423
If I ever talk on the phone at home again,
I'm the son of the dog next door.

120
00:09:17,845 --> 00:09:19,460
Why did I do that?

121
00:09:19,787 --> 00:09:22,697
That little kid has sharp ears, though.

122
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,866
What's with that face?
Did something happen?

123
00:09:36,233 --> 00:09:39,728
You look like you just
had it out with Dad.

124
00:09:40,013 --> 00:09:41,167
Let's just go to school.

125
00:09:41,433 --> 00:09:44,313
Why fight with Dad?
You'll only drive yourself crazy.

126
00:09:44,338 --> 00:09:46,743
Why? What happened this time?

127
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:48,937
Hey, Han Gyu Seo!

128
00:09:55,346 --> 00:09:58,041
What? Is it because Dad has a girlfriend?

129
00:09:58,547 --> 00:09:59,659
How did you know?

130
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:02,835
- How did you know?
- It'd be weirder not to know.

131
00:10:02,927 --> 00:10:05,230
He's showing it off like a total fool.

132
00:10:06,086 --> 00:10:08,272
Why is our dad such an embarrassment?

133
00:10:08,446 --> 00:10:10,126
We're always the ones left embarrassed.

134
00:10:10,733 --> 00:10:13,359
But I bet older women find Dad charming.

135
00:10:13,494 --> 00:10:15,859
He looks super young,
he looks good in clothes,

136
00:10:15,884 --> 00:10:18,673
and he's optimistic and innocent
about everything. Like a kid.

137
00:10:19,567 --> 00:10:23,575
He's cute sometimes. Cover his eyes,
and he's Jo In Sung for half a second.

138
00:10:26,837 --> 00:10:28,427
I regretted it as soon as I said it.

139
00:10:29,987 --> 00:10:33,210
- You're off work today, right?
- Yeah. Why?

140
00:10:33,827 --> 00:10:35,087
Let's go see the lady.

141
00:10:35,749 --> 00:10:37,905
- The lady?
- Gyu Rim's mom.

142
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:40,219
You like her that much?

143
00:10:40,526 --> 00:10:42,532
What do you like so much about her?

144
00:10:43,586 --> 00:10:46,487
I don't know. She's warm.

145
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:49,057
Why? Are you cold?

146
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:54,224
- What?
- I know you followed us, so come out.

147
00:10:54,651 --> 00:10:55,960
Who followed us?

148
00:10:56,593 --> 00:10:58,417
Stop hiding and come out.

149
00:10:58,573 --> 00:11:00,142
I heard your steps.

150
00:11:26,546 --> 00:11:29,974
So who's the fan?
Your daughter, or you, ma'am?

151
00:11:32,753 --> 00:11:35,600
Well, you see...

152
00:11:38,734 --> 00:11:41,634
Me. I'm the fan.

153
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,167
Would you like an autograph? Or a photo?

154
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:48,454
A photo! Please take a photo with me.

155
00:11:52,125 --> 00:11:53,260
Here.

156
00:11:55,666 --> 00:11:58,168
Here we go. One, two.

157
00:11:58,193 --> 00:12:01,839
Wait. Could this young lady
be in the picture too?

158
00:12:03,109 --> 00:12:05,396
- Me?
- Yes, you.

159
00:12:05,490 --> 00:12:07,600
You two look like twins.

160
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,442
How did you know we're twins?

161
00:12:13,147 --> 00:12:14,686
She must be your obsessive fan.

162
00:12:16,095 --> 00:12:17,807
You and Han Gyu Seo go ahead.

163
00:12:17,832 --> 00:12:19,752
He's the model. I'm just a regular person.

164
00:12:20,327 --> 00:12:22,688
Come on, let's all take one together.

165
00:12:23,787 --> 00:12:25,358
We have to hurry to school.

166
00:12:25,526 --> 00:12:26,846
Let's just take one of the two of us.

167
00:12:27,114 --> 00:12:31,861
You look so much like the daughter
I lost when she was little.

168
00:12:32,593 --> 00:12:36,035
Please take just one with me
and pretend I'm your mom.

169
00:12:37,007 --> 00:12:38,714
What's with this stalker fan lady?

170
00:12:38,739 --> 00:12:40,007
Do something.

171
00:12:40,256 --> 00:12:41,819
She doesn't like having her picture taken.

172
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:43,247
Let's just take one of the two of us.

173
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:51,360
Hey, come here.
Let's take one with her, okay?

174
00:12:54,162 --> 00:12:56,940
Link arms too. Now, look over here.

175
00:12:56,965 --> 00:12:59,613
One, two, three. Smile.

176
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:03,207
One more. Smile.

177
00:13:31,359 --> 00:13:32,695
You're awake?

178
00:13:33,623 --> 00:13:35,630
How are you feeling?

179
00:13:37,945 --> 00:13:39,167
I'm fine.

180
00:13:41,713 --> 00:13:45,115
They said it was stress-induced cramps.

181
00:13:45,512 --> 00:13:51,002
I thought you were tough as nails,
that nothing could ever rattle you,

182
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:53,977
but I guess you do get stressed out?

183
00:13:55,067 --> 00:13:56,660
This is so humiliating.

184
00:13:57,446 --> 00:13:59,165
Yeah. You must be embarrassed.

185
00:13:59,190 --> 00:14:01,765
Totally humiliating.

186
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:07,120
You bragged to your family
like you were marrying royalty...

187
00:14:07,145 --> 00:14:10,058
and made such a huge fuss.

188
00:14:10,514 --> 00:14:12,541
You must be mortified.

189
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:15,477
Even I'm embarrassed for you.

190
00:14:16,535 --> 00:14:18,033
Why did you bring me to the hospital?

191
00:14:18,273 --> 00:14:21,373
Why didn't you just let me die of shame?
Why did you bring me to the hospital?

192
00:14:22,454 --> 00:14:23,694
So it's my fault again?

193
00:14:24,890 --> 00:14:26,819
Don't tell my family.

194
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:28,893
If you so much as breathe a word,

195
00:14:28,918 --> 00:14:30,754
I won't let you get away with it.
I'll destroy you.

196
00:14:30,813 --> 00:14:33,129
I wouldn't, even if you asked me to.

197
00:14:33,666 --> 00:14:36,886
If Gyu Rim knew you'd ended up like this,
she'd faint.

198
00:14:38,854 --> 00:14:41,042
Faint? Yeah, right.

199
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:43,897
"Serves her right. Good riddance.
She had it coming."

200
00:14:44,326 --> 00:14:47,521
She'd be so thrilled she'd faint.

201
00:14:48,152 --> 00:14:54,706
Of all the people I know,
you're the second-meanest in the country.

202
00:14:55,907 --> 00:14:57,766
Your husband Seong Uk is number one.

203
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,932
Have you heard from Kang Seong Uk?

204
00:15:01,957 --> 00:15:03,749
Of course I have.

205
00:15:03,947 --> 00:15:05,171
He wants to know where you are.

206
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:08,509
He says he knows you and I are together.
He's called me 100 times.

207
00:15:09,167 --> 00:15:11,202
And you turned off your phone.

208
00:15:14,065 --> 00:15:17,386
Why? What is it?

209
00:15:18,434 --> 00:15:22,794
Besides cheating and his paranoia,
what else is there?

210
00:15:23,194 --> 00:15:25,861
Tell me. What is it?

211
00:15:29,708 --> 00:15:31,154
Hide me, please.

212
00:15:31,906 --> 00:15:33,667
What are you talking about?

213
00:15:33,692 --> 00:15:36,423
Hide me somewhere that jerk
can never find me.

214
00:15:36,448 --> 00:15:38,157
So he won't find a single trace of me.

215
00:15:39,293 --> 00:15:41,613
Where am I supposed to hide a grown woman?

216
00:15:41,747 --> 00:15:45,128
If you were the size of a peanut,
I'd carry you around in my pocket.

217
00:15:46,247 --> 00:15:49,974
If you won't even hide me,
then why did you save me?

218
00:15:49,999 --> 00:15:53,059
Why didn't you just let me die?
Why did you bring me to the hospital?

219
00:15:55,847 --> 00:15:59,686
Why didn't you try harder to stop me
from marrying Kang Seong Uk?

220
00:16:00,099 --> 00:16:02,576
You said Seong Uk really looked up to you,

221
00:16:02,658 --> 00:16:05,041
so how could you not know
he was such a jerk? Why?

222
00:16:05,066 --> 00:16:07,472
How could you not know? How?

223
00:16:08,055 --> 00:16:10,662
Give me strength.

224
00:16:11,755 --> 00:16:16,091
What am I supposed to do with this lamb
who's gone completely off the rails?

225
00:16:17,225 --> 00:16:18,738
Give me patience.

226
00:16:25,806 --> 00:16:29,465
You asked me to have lunch with you,
and you already ate without me?

227
00:16:30,898 --> 00:16:32,657
I'll eat something super tasty after.

228
00:16:32,759 --> 00:16:34,471
You said we'd eat together.

229
00:16:36,216 --> 00:16:37,943
With everyone watching,
I'm getting nervous.

230
00:16:43,811 --> 00:16:46,559
- Very good.
- Nice shot.

231
00:16:49,534 --> 00:16:51,202
I don't think I'll make the qualifiers.

232
00:16:52,273 --> 00:16:55,729
How many teams made it to the finals
this year again?

233
00:16:55,754 --> 00:16:57,462
Yes, 14 teams in total.

234
00:16:57,526 --> 00:16:59,222
That's two more than last year.

235
00:16:59,939 --> 00:17:01,282
I see. Okay.

236
00:17:02,055 --> 00:17:05,235
But seeing it all in person,

237
00:17:05,939 --> 00:17:07,679
I love this fall line's colors.

238
00:17:08,159 --> 00:17:10,339
- Very good.
- Yes.

239
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:13,573
Those young men over there
look really sharp, like models.

240
00:17:13,611 --> 00:17:15,816
- Do our clothes make them look good?
- Of course.

241
00:17:15,841 --> 00:17:16,874
- Sir.
- Yes.

242
00:17:22,703 --> 00:17:23,796
That'll do.

243
00:17:30,977 --> 00:17:35,219
Then get ready for tomorrow's contest.
Go ahead and get back to work.

244
00:17:35,264 --> 00:17:36,895
Yes, sir.

245
00:17:37,026 --> 00:17:38,675
- This way, please.
- Okay.

246
00:17:50,336 --> 00:17:51,557
Keep up the good work.

247
00:17:53,025 --> 00:17:54,253
- Thank you.
- Sure.

248
00:17:54,278 --> 00:17:56,757
Hello, sir.

249
00:17:56,782 --> 00:17:58,508
Hello.

250
00:18:00,938 --> 00:18:02,500
- Hello.
- Hi.

251
00:18:03,132 --> 00:18:04,804
Our clothes look really good on you.

252
00:18:04,829 --> 00:18:06,897
You could model for our company.

253
00:18:07,974 --> 00:18:09,489
- Thank you.
- Sure.

254
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:12,021
Wait a moment.

255
00:18:13,248 --> 00:18:14,782
Well...

256
00:18:16,558 --> 00:18:18,167
Reach out whenever you have time.

257
00:18:18,192 --> 00:18:20,185
Let's have a meal together.

258
00:18:25,053 --> 00:18:30,241
I'm sorry, but I don't eat
with people I don't know.

259
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:32,234
I'm sorry.

260
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,403
Let's go.

261
00:18:39,806 --> 00:18:43,593
Sir, I'll make sure he calls you.

262
00:18:58,091 --> 00:18:59,599
Hey, why did you take that?

263
00:18:59,958 --> 00:19:01,920
There's no reason for me
to eat with the chairman.

264
00:19:02,486 --> 00:19:05,228
Hey, you've got to make things happen.

265
00:19:05,253 --> 00:19:09,894
Everyone else is desperate
just to make eye contact with him.

266
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:15,077
Forget it. I'm not interested,
so go yourself if you want.

267
00:19:17,039 --> 00:19:19,242
You're so frustrating, I swear.

268
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:22,799
Hey, take this and go ahead.

269
00:19:26,133 --> 00:19:29,648
Anyway, I saved the chairman's number,
just so you know.

270
00:19:32,646 --> 00:19:35,025
Drink some iced coffee
and have a great day.

271
00:19:35,553 --> 00:19:39,256
Don't forget something sweet too.
Let's get a little sweeter, Han Gyu O.

272
00:19:43,139 --> 00:19:44,694
What am I to you?

273
00:19:46,219 --> 00:19:49,277
You said no other woman
meant anything to you but me.

274
00:19:49,724 --> 00:19:51,270
You said I was the only one.

275
00:19:51,533 --> 00:19:53,404
So how can you treat me like this?

276
00:19:55,174 --> 00:19:59,350
If we hadn't run into each other today,
were you never going to see me again?

277
00:20:03,253 --> 00:20:06,186
You've heard of the woman who waited
so long she turned to stone, right?

278
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:10,054
I almost turned to stone waiting for you.

279
00:20:10,434 --> 00:20:14,937
In class the other day,
I even said four times nine was 49.

280
00:20:16,479 --> 00:20:18,997
I feel like I've turned this much to stone
because of you,

281
00:20:19,144 --> 00:20:20,824
so how are you going to make it up to me?

282
00:20:23,174 --> 00:20:25,103
Who am I even talking to right now?

283
00:20:26,557 --> 00:20:27,820
Who do you think you are?

284
00:20:28,467 --> 00:20:33,042
I'm asking you all these questions,
and you won't say a word.

285
00:20:34,907 --> 00:20:37,089
You're curious about so much,

286
00:20:38,630 --> 00:20:41,856
so why have you never asked what I do?

287
00:20:43,832 --> 00:20:44,878
What?

288
00:20:45,113 --> 00:20:50,706
Aren't you curious what kind of guy I am,
or what I do for a living?

289
00:20:52,126 --> 00:20:55,907
No. I don't care if you're unemployed.

290
00:20:57,559 --> 00:20:59,251
I used to be a host bar escort.

291
00:21:06,312 --> 00:21:07,487
Scared?

292
00:21:14,307 --> 00:21:19,275
"Used to be." So that's past tense.

293
00:21:21,351 --> 00:21:22,886
Not present tense.

294
00:21:25,139 --> 00:21:26,273
You're not shocked?

295
00:21:27,053 --> 00:21:30,322
I was shocked to death. In the past tense.

296
00:21:31,592 --> 00:21:34,760
- What?
- The past doesn't matter.

297
00:21:35,373 --> 00:21:37,358
What's done is done. Why would it matter?

298
00:21:38,352 --> 00:21:40,319
Present tense, that's what matters.

299
00:21:40,527 --> 00:21:44,330
If you said you were a host
bar escort now, I'd kill you.

300
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:47,416
I don't care about your past.

301
00:21:47,634 --> 00:21:49,243
So what are you now?

302
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:56,600
Did you love me, or do you love me?

303
00:21:58,613 --> 00:22:01,282
Is it past tense or present tense?

304
00:22:01,890 --> 00:22:03,270
You won't answer?

305
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,252
I'm going to sulk. I mean it.

306
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:35,359
I love you. Present tense.

307
00:22:35,643 --> 00:22:38,776
Present tense!

308
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:55,691
I'm sorry I haven't come to see you
in so long.

309
00:22:56,817 --> 00:22:58,237
I was wrong.

310
00:23:02,359 --> 00:23:03,947
Did you change tactics?

311
00:23:04,355 --> 00:23:07,122
Did Han Gyu Rim tell you to come
and beg no matter what?

312
00:23:07,959 --> 00:23:09,845
I want to make up with you, Mother.

313
00:23:10,666 --> 00:23:12,634
I asked if Han Gyu Rim put you up to this.

314
00:23:13,861 --> 00:23:16,361
I asked if she sent you.

315
00:23:18,224 --> 00:23:21,384
- Yes.
- What?

316
00:23:22,380 --> 00:23:27,629
She told me to make up with you
and come back with your permission.

317
00:23:29,719 --> 00:23:33,439
Get up.

318
00:23:34,205 --> 00:23:36,091
Get up!

319
00:23:37,357 --> 00:23:40,437
Get up!

320
00:23:40,765 --> 00:23:42,418
Get up, you fool!

321
00:23:43,661 --> 00:23:49,964
You fool, you're on your knees like this
over some girl?

322
00:23:49,989 --> 00:23:52,372
Is this what I get...

323
00:23:52,700 --> 00:23:57,427
for having you, feeding you, clothing you,
and putting you through school?

324
00:23:59,307 --> 00:24:00,629
I was wrong.

325
00:24:01,056 --> 00:24:07,016
Even if you were wrong,
I shouldn't have left home like that.

326
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:09,526
Did you just say I was wrong?

327
00:24:09,929 --> 00:24:12,727
What was I wrong about?

328
00:24:17,380 --> 00:24:20,614
You always said what matters most
in the world is a person's character,

329
00:24:20,821 --> 00:24:24,875
but you only looked at her appearance
and her background.

330
00:24:25,020 --> 00:24:30,124
You judged her by what the world values,
jumped to conclusions, and shut her out.

331
00:24:31,460 --> 00:24:33,865
Is Han Gyu Rim really that great?

332
00:24:34,966 --> 00:24:37,598
Is she really that wonderful?

333
00:24:38,546 --> 00:24:41,499
How did that girl bewitch you so badly...

334
00:24:42,293 --> 00:24:47,098
that you, my brilliant son,
can't even think straight anymore?

335
00:24:47,129 --> 00:24:48,740
Please, Mother.

336
00:24:49,142 --> 00:24:54,662
It's my life to live.
Can't you just trust me?

337
00:24:55,333 --> 00:25:00,494
Can't you trust me just this once?

338
00:25:00,573 --> 00:25:02,587
Just give Gyu Rim a hug once,

339
00:25:02,612 --> 00:25:07,854
and accept her just once
as the woman I love,

340
00:25:08,634 --> 00:25:11,608
and I'll never ask you for anything again
for the rest of my life.

341
00:25:27,947 --> 00:25:33,463
Six kilos each of potatoes and onions,
four of zucchini, and five of cucumbers.

342
00:25:33,597 --> 00:25:35,317
And how are the bellflower roots?

343
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:39,217
Last time they were dried out and mushy.
You know they weren't great, right?

344
00:25:40,133 --> 00:25:43,176
Okay, then about four kilos of those too.

345
00:25:47,733 --> 00:25:50,558
Okay, thanks so much.

346
00:25:53,279 --> 00:25:57,924
- You're back to normal today.
- Yes.

347
00:25:58,948 --> 00:26:01,806
We open for business in two days.

348
00:26:02,341 --> 00:26:04,770
Isn't Su Nam here?

349
00:26:04,870 --> 00:26:07,570
She doesn't run the side dish shop now.

350
00:26:07,637 --> 00:26:12,537
She left this place to me
and runs the shop across from here.

351
00:26:12,570 --> 00:26:13,970
I see.

352
00:26:19,270 --> 00:26:25,703
You don't have multiple personalities
like Jekyll and Hyde, do you?

353
00:26:26,970 --> 00:26:28,803
No, I don't.

354
00:26:30,937 --> 00:26:34,037
You know Mu Jin went
to see his mother today, right?

355
00:26:35,737 --> 00:26:40,203
So you didn't know.
He took a day off to go see her.

356
00:26:40,670 --> 00:26:45,837
He says he'll get permission to see you,
no matter what, and settle this for good.

357
00:26:48,603 --> 00:26:52,903
His mother's no ordinary woman,
and Mu Jin's no ordinary guy either.

358
00:26:53,503 --> 00:26:55,470
Maybe I should get an ambulance ready.

359
00:27:02,903 --> 00:27:04,903
What brings you all the way here?

360
00:27:06,537 --> 00:27:09,737
Last time, you left without even eating.

361
00:27:09,863 --> 00:27:13,330
I even made you something special,
and someone else got to enjoy it.

362
00:27:14,370 --> 00:27:15,803
Have a seat first.

363
00:27:17,103 --> 00:27:21,437
Something came up, and I had to step out.

364
00:27:21,737 --> 00:27:24,803
Whether it went in their mouths or mine,
it's all the same,

365
00:27:24,870 --> 00:27:26,137
so don't feel bad about it.

366
00:27:26,337 --> 00:27:28,134
Still, I was a little hurt.

367
00:27:28,159 --> 00:27:31,175
So I made some lasagna,

368
00:27:31,368 --> 00:27:35,103
thinking you'd like it,
and wrapped it up for you.

369
00:27:35,128 --> 00:27:37,549
- Lasagna?
- It's lasagna.

370
00:27:38,337 --> 00:27:40,270
Mr. Song, do you know what this is?

371
00:27:40,303 --> 00:27:45,303
Of course. It's a kind of Italian pasta.
It's really delicious and expensive.

372
00:27:45,337 --> 00:27:50,270
It's nothing. You really know your stuff.

373
00:27:51,403 --> 00:27:55,737
Goodness, we've barely met.

374
00:27:56,070 --> 00:27:58,437
You're so thoughtful.

375
00:27:59,970 --> 00:28:04,303
On Maenggoldo, an island near Jindo,

376
00:28:04,503 --> 00:28:07,337
there's a lovely girl
who harvests rock seaweed.

377
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:12,103
Should I play matchmaker?

378
00:28:12,737 --> 00:28:15,237
What a shame.

379
00:28:15,337 --> 00:28:20,470
I didn't know there was such a good match,
and I went on a blind date not long ago.

380
00:28:21,803 --> 00:28:24,132
She's from Jeopdo, near Jindo,

381
00:28:24,251 --> 00:28:27,205
and I'm going down to meet her parents
next month.

382
00:28:28,770 --> 00:28:34,137
Jeopdo women are so capable,
they say men marry them sight unseen.

383
00:28:34,370 --> 00:28:37,103
Things have already moved that fast?

384
00:28:37,137 --> 00:28:42,403
Well, my father's health
suddenly got worse...

385
00:28:42,703 --> 00:28:47,337
He really wants to see me
get married before he dies.

386
00:28:47,803 --> 00:28:53,137
What a devoted son.
I've never seen one like you these days.

387
00:28:53,170 --> 00:29:00,142
I gave him so much grief when I was young,
and now that I can finally be a good son,

388
00:29:02,537 --> 00:29:04,703
he's talking about dying...

389
00:29:07,703 --> 00:29:10,103
It's breaking my heart.

390
00:29:10,737 --> 00:29:16,837
Right. Parents don't wait forever
for their kids to take care of them.

391
00:29:19,803 --> 00:29:21,551
That gives me an idea.

392
00:29:21,765 --> 00:29:24,418
Should I try conning my Heung Sik?

393
00:29:25,270 --> 00:29:29,070
"The doctor says I don't have
long to live."

394
00:29:29,137 --> 00:29:31,470
That's the white lie I'll tell Heung Sik.

395
00:29:31,503 --> 00:29:34,670
"So give me a grandkid."

396
00:29:45,129 --> 00:29:47,041
Is this even food?

397
00:29:49,562 --> 00:29:52,521
Can't you go out and get me
some spicy chicken feet?

398
00:29:53,437 --> 00:29:56,495
You want to wreck your stomach again
after they barely got it treated?

399
00:29:56,715 --> 00:29:58,509
Just eat what you're given.

400
00:30:00,770 --> 00:30:03,835
- I'm getting discharged tonight, right?
- Yeah.

401
00:30:12,370 --> 00:30:15,703
Hey, what if Seong Uk calls
when you turn your phone on?

402
00:30:16,803 --> 00:30:18,937
I'll make one call and turn it right off.

403
00:30:24,837 --> 00:30:27,287
- Hey, Se Hui.
- What's going on with you?

404
00:30:27,503 --> 00:30:30,570
Do you know how many times I called
and texted you?

405
00:30:31,270 --> 00:30:32,870
Sorry, something came up.

406
00:30:34,203 --> 00:30:37,137
Your husband came to the office
looking for you.

407
00:30:37,837 --> 00:30:40,070
I think he's still waiting outside.

408
00:30:40,170 --> 00:30:42,265
He came to the office?

409
00:30:42,619 --> 00:30:47,299
He's still outside? That psycho.

410
00:30:48,837 --> 00:30:53,437
Se Hui, I don't want to see that jerk,

411
00:30:53,637 --> 00:30:55,403
so can I stay with you for a few days?

412
00:30:55,737 --> 00:30:57,570
I'm scared he'll follow me to a hotel.

413
00:30:57,837 --> 00:30:59,871
Your husband knows where I live.

414
00:31:00,098 --> 00:31:02,812
Then it's not safe there either.

415
00:31:03,270 --> 00:31:06,743
Right. That jerk knows where you live too.

416
00:31:08,670 --> 00:31:10,070
(Not My Husband)

417
00:31:10,803 --> 00:31:13,407
Hey, that jerk is calling me.
I'll hang up for now.

418
00:31:15,537 --> 00:31:17,670
He's staking out the office?

419
00:31:17,824 --> 00:31:19,584
What on earth is going on with you two?

420
00:31:20,137 --> 00:31:22,703
Nobody plays hide-and-seek this viciously.

421
00:31:22,737 --> 00:31:26,003
It is hide-and-seek.
If he catches me, I'm dead.

422
00:31:27,670 --> 00:31:30,937
What do I do? Should I hire a bodyguard?

423
00:31:35,903 --> 00:31:39,303
Did you forget? One punch, six teeth.

424
00:31:41,970 --> 00:31:43,303
I'll protect you.

425
00:31:44,137 --> 00:31:48,703
That's right. His natural enemy
was right next to me all along.

426
00:31:49,537 --> 00:31:52,003
I'm saved.

427
00:31:54,303 --> 00:31:57,337
What kind of girl are you,
throwing yourself at a man like that?

428
00:31:57,603 --> 00:32:00,137
No wonder people suspect an affair.

429
00:32:01,103 --> 00:32:02,879
Since when are you a man?

430
00:32:03,113 --> 00:32:06,733
You said we're all descendants of Dangun.

431
00:32:06,937 --> 00:32:10,103
That even strangers hugged each other
during the 2002 World Cup.

432
00:32:12,003 --> 00:32:13,270
You startled me.

433
00:32:25,269 --> 00:32:29,797
Mu Jin, do you know you've been like this
for three hours?

434
00:32:31,437 --> 00:32:35,087
Just sitting is hard enough,
and you're even on your knees.

435
00:32:35,501 --> 00:32:37,115
Just go home for today.

436
00:32:37,496 --> 00:32:41,796
Go home today, and come back
another day to beg.

437
00:32:45,037 --> 00:32:47,637
I told you Mom left work early today.

438
00:32:49,037 --> 00:32:51,837
Hey, staying like this won't do any good.

439
00:33:06,137 --> 00:33:09,303
You know Mu Jin went
to see his mother today, right?

440
00:33:09,637 --> 00:33:14,070
He says he'll get permission to see you,
no matter what, and settle this for good.

441
00:33:17,996 --> 00:33:19,391
There you are.

442
00:33:19,632 --> 00:33:24,419
I went to my son-in-law Kim's restaurant,
but they said he didn't come in today.

443
00:33:28,970 --> 00:33:30,337
Please accept my apology.

444
00:33:34,803 --> 00:33:40,003
If I'd known Gyeol was listening,
I'd have to be crazy to say that.

445
00:33:40,437 --> 00:33:44,870
I've grown so attached to Gyeol
that he really feels like my grandson now.

446
00:33:45,870 --> 00:33:48,270
He doesn't just feel like it.
He is your grandson.

447
00:33:51,503 --> 00:33:53,937
This mouth of mine, honestly...

448
00:33:54,576 --> 00:33:58,043
How many times will I get hit today,
Han Seok Jung?

449
00:33:59,155 --> 00:34:03,955
Look here. I've got a bump, right?

450
00:34:06,337 --> 00:34:10,703
I hated myself so much, I hit myself
on the head really hard today.

451
00:34:10,737 --> 00:34:13,270
I've got a bump right here. Feel it.

452
00:34:16,170 --> 00:34:17,470
I've got a girlfriend.

453
00:34:22,237 --> 00:34:23,823
Is it the real deal this time?

454
00:34:25,003 --> 00:34:26,237
How did you know?

455
00:34:27,603 --> 00:34:31,270
I'm wondering whether to just stay friends
and keep flirting,

456
00:34:32,770 --> 00:34:37,037
or go all the way and get married.

457
00:34:38,103 --> 00:34:40,103
Do whatever you want, Dad. It's your life.

458
00:34:40,128 --> 00:34:44,828
Do you want to go first? Or should I?

459
00:34:47,770 --> 00:34:52,670
Hey, what if...

460
00:34:53,543 --> 00:34:57,557
we both end up getting married?
How about a joint wedding?

461
00:35:01,337 --> 00:35:06,770
You think I want to get married at my age
for my own sake?

462
00:35:07,070 --> 00:35:11,737
Not in a million years.
It's all for you kids.

463
00:35:12,103 --> 00:35:17,137
Taking care of a sick, old man like me
is no easy job.

464
00:35:17,403 --> 00:35:21,770
I'm passing off this burden called Dad
to your new stepmom,

465
00:35:22,203 --> 00:35:27,503
so you kids can live comfortably.
That's how thoughtful I am.

466
00:35:29,170 --> 00:35:32,103
Even I'm touched by what I just said.

467
00:35:32,437 --> 00:35:35,370
Hey, aren't I such a cool,
wonderful father?

468
00:35:38,137 --> 00:35:39,403
Who is she?

469
00:35:41,270 --> 00:35:43,903
She's two years older than me,
and she owns a sashimi restaurant.

470
00:35:44,103 --> 00:35:47,303
She's so innocent.
Not a speck of dirt on her.

471
00:35:47,537 --> 00:35:50,870
Her son seems to give her a lot of grief,

472
00:35:51,070 --> 00:35:53,508
so I think that's why we get along.

473
00:35:53,855 --> 00:35:56,262
I know that pain better than anyone.

474
00:35:57,630 --> 00:36:00,633
Does she want to marry you too?

475
00:36:01,003 --> 00:36:04,837
Of course she does.
She's completely crazy about me.

476
00:36:04,903 --> 00:36:07,003
Did you tell her all about yourself?

477
00:36:07,837 --> 00:36:09,837
Did you tell her why Mom left home,

478
00:36:09,903 --> 00:36:13,903
and that this would be
your third marriage?

479
00:36:15,070 --> 00:36:16,137
I think so?

480
00:36:16,703 --> 00:36:21,670
And did you tell her how incompetent
and irresponsible you are?

481
00:36:22,903 --> 00:36:24,503
Yes, I told her everything.

482
00:36:24,737 --> 00:36:28,703
That I'm unemployed and a total slacker.
I told her everything. So what?

483
00:36:29,303 --> 00:36:31,165
Like I said earlier,

484
00:36:31,852 --> 00:36:34,486
it's your life,
so live it however you want.

485
00:36:35,337 --> 00:36:36,937
Just don't hurt the kids.

486
00:36:38,103 --> 00:36:40,303
Do you think I hurt them on purpose?

487
00:36:40,537 --> 00:36:43,170
That's why I'm asking you
to talk to them for me.

488
00:36:49,070 --> 00:36:51,370
Would you like to meet my Ms. Hong?

489
00:36:59,603 --> 00:37:03,695
Anyway, you're in favor
of me getting married.

490
00:37:04,097 --> 00:37:06,972
If you're against it, speak up
before I count to ten.

491
00:37:08,103 --> 00:37:11,604
Two, four, six, eight, ten.
You're in favor.

492
00:37:15,369 --> 00:37:21,169
Tell the kids I didn't want to,
but you pushed me into it.

493
00:37:22,103 --> 00:37:27,003
Let's say you didn't want to look after me
and dumped me on your stepmom.

494
00:37:28,570 --> 00:37:29,603
Got it?

495
00:37:32,103 --> 00:37:37,337
Hey, what's with your outfit today?
Even your necklace looks like a kid's...

496
00:37:37,362 --> 00:37:38,778
Pretty, right?

497
00:37:39,137 --> 00:37:40,537
Yes, it's pretty.

498
00:37:42,903 --> 00:37:45,603
What's all this?
Did you make it all yourself?

499
00:37:45,644 --> 00:37:50,283
The rice cooker made the rice,
and my eldest daughter made the kimchi.

500
00:37:50,308 --> 00:37:51,901
I just scooped it out.

501
00:38:02,803 --> 00:38:07,703
It's delicious. Seriously,
it's insanely good.

502
00:38:10,070 --> 00:38:15,437
You said you love home cooking
and can eat three bowls with good kimchi,

503
00:38:15,537 --> 00:38:18,637
so I dug out every kind of kimchi
in the house and brought it.

504
00:38:23,637 --> 00:38:29,903
Your eldest daughter's cooking
is like a five-star hotel chef's...

505
00:38:30,176 --> 00:38:34,176
It's way better than my head chef's.
A hundred times better.

506
00:38:34,237 --> 00:38:36,421
- Is it that good?
- Yeah.

507
00:38:36,670 --> 00:38:41,437
I eat kimchi at home all the time,
so I never really noticed.

508
00:38:41,737 --> 00:38:44,770
What does your eldest daughter do?
Is she a chef?

509
00:38:45,343 --> 00:38:46,537
Something like that.

510
00:38:46,570 --> 00:38:51,237
Yeah, I knew it.
This isn't amateur cooking. Really...

511
00:38:55,037 --> 00:38:59,470
It's delicious. Is your daughter married?

512
00:39:00,737 --> 00:39:03,837
She will be soon. She's seeing someone.

513
00:39:06,837 --> 00:39:08,436
What a lucky guy.

514
00:39:09,104 --> 00:39:13,537
If she weren't taken,
I'd snatch her up as my daughter-in-law.

515
00:39:14,203 --> 00:39:18,503
If my daughter is your daughter-in-law,
then what does that make us?

516
00:39:20,770 --> 00:39:22,437
We'd be in-laws, then?

517
00:39:24,823 --> 00:39:27,712
Why so serious? I was just joking.

518
00:39:29,437 --> 00:39:31,337
You scared me.

519
00:39:35,537 --> 00:39:39,172
Tuna is always delicious.

520
00:39:39,303 --> 00:39:41,770
It's good when you eat out,
and it's good at home too.

521
00:39:44,037 --> 00:39:45,603
- Seok Jung.
- Yeah?

522
00:39:49,137 --> 00:39:52,370
Tell me. Do you see me as a woman?

523
00:39:54,870 --> 00:39:56,537
Well, you're a woman, not a man, right?

524
00:39:57,403 --> 00:40:00,870
No, I'm serious.

525
00:40:08,137 --> 00:40:09,970
I feel the same way you do.

526
00:40:12,137 --> 00:40:14,975
If you see me as a friend,
then I'm your friend,

527
00:40:15,595 --> 00:40:18,849
and if you see me as a man,
then you're a woman to me.

528
00:40:22,537 --> 00:40:27,170
Right? That's how it is, right, Seok Jung?

529
00:40:29,003 --> 00:40:30,637
Maybe she hasn't fallen for me yet?

530
00:40:35,837 --> 00:40:38,903
Of course, we're friends.

531
00:40:40,103 --> 00:40:41,137
Yeah.

532
00:40:42,503 --> 00:40:44,137
- We're friends.
- Yeah.

533
00:40:47,703 --> 00:40:52,970
<i>My friend my friend what is time</i>

534
00:40:53,503 --> 00:40:58,070
<i>What is time</i>

535
00:40:58,603 --> 00:41:03,137
<i>On the road we've traveled</i>

536
00:41:03,670 --> 00:41:07,570
<i>The two of us met</i>

537
00:41:10,470 --> 00:41:15,124
- Hey, you'd better be careful.
- About what?

538
00:41:15,837 --> 00:41:20,703
That look.
That look gives me the wrong idea.

539
00:41:22,137 --> 00:41:24,637
That look, like you're under my spell.

540
00:41:26,670 --> 00:41:31,137
That look makes me wonder,
"Did she fall for me?" It confuses me.

541
00:41:38,503 --> 00:41:39,870
Should we just stop seeing each other?

542
00:41:41,270 --> 00:41:45,770
I don't have much life left,
and I don't even have time to meet women.

543
00:41:46,037 --> 00:41:48,403
I don't have time to goof around
with a friend like this.

544
00:41:49,637 --> 00:41:51,337
I have to go,
so hurry up and eat your lunch.

545
00:41:52,437 --> 00:41:57,837
Seok Jung.

546
00:42:00,037 --> 00:42:03,870
Even my suit got torn.
Do you know how expensive this is?

547
00:42:04,503 --> 00:42:09,737
Sir, what kind of training
do you give your staff?

548
00:42:10,003 --> 00:42:15,170
Some lowly grunt had the nerve
to lay a hand on the chairman's in-law...

549
00:42:16,337 --> 00:42:19,437
Call right now and fire those punks.

550
00:42:22,237 --> 00:42:26,970
He just did his job. Why would I fire him?
I should be praising him.

551
00:42:28,303 --> 00:42:30,670
So you're going to be like that?

552
00:42:32,883 --> 00:42:37,283
Then maybe I should play hardball too.

553
00:42:37,737 --> 00:42:42,737
Now, where is it?
I'm not sure if you remember,

554
00:42:43,803 --> 00:42:48,970
but after you posed as Han Seok Jung,

555
00:42:49,070 --> 00:42:53,670
this is what you said
at our families' meeting. Here it is.

556
00:42:57,803 --> 00:43:03,337
Hello, sir. I'm Seong Uk's father,
Kang Sang Man.

557
00:43:03,837 --> 00:43:05,437
That's my voice.

558
00:43:05,470 --> 00:43:09,470
Yes, nice to meet you.
I'm Gyu Yeong's father, Han Seok Jung.

559
00:43:12,637 --> 00:43:17,837
You clearly said Han Seok Jung,
not Jang Hun Tae.

560
00:43:18,970 --> 00:43:21,303
Isn't this what they call a smoking gun?

561
00:43:22,403 --> 00:43:26,437
My son asked ChatGPT or whatever,

562
00:43:27,037 --> 00:43:30,070
the thing that's way smarter than people,

563
00:43:31,203 --> 00:43:34,603
and apparently impersonating someone
violates some article in the Criminal Act,

564
00:43:34,903 --> 00:43:37,270
and if you commit a crime,
you should be punished.

565
00:43:37,970 --> 00:43:43,170
Why? You want to do this by the book?
If you want a legal fight, go ahead.

566
00:43:43,837 --> 00:43:45,570
- Are you sure you'll be okay?
- Yes.

567
00:43:45,870 --> 00:43:50,937
There's your image and the company's name.
You have a lot to protect.

568
00:43:51,037 --> 00:43:54,570
Well, I'm not sure what I have to protect,

569
00:43:54,903 --> 00:43:59,437
but if there's anything,
it's my family I should protect first.

570
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:00,861
Exactly.

571
00:44:01,101 --> 00:44:05,381
So why does a family man like you
keep barking up the wrong tree?

572
00:44:05,803 --> 00:44:08,303
What do you think would happen
if I posted this online?

573
00:44:08,403 --> 00:44:11,670
First of all, Gyu Yeong would be finished.

574
00:44:13,003 --> 00:44:15,283
And I hear you have a daughter
of your own.

575
00:44:16,083 --> 00:44:19,349
Haven't you thought about
what that would do to her?

576
00:44:20,137 --> 00:44:27,003
Plus, how humiliated would your wife be,
the one Gyu Yeong said was dead?

577
00:44:28,337 --> 00:44:34,503
We'll post every detail about your wife's
divorce and remarriage,

578
00:44:34,903 --> 00:44:39,237
so wouldn't she be too ashamed
to show her face anywhere in Korea?

579
00:44:42,870 --> 00:44:47,503
For people like us,
three convictions or four, four or five,

580
00:44:47,570 --> 00:44:49,837
it's all the same.

581
00:44:50,170 --> 00:44:54,270
These days, people even eat prison food
on purpose for their health.

582
00:44:57,970 --> 00:45:02,737
Someone told me money is the easiest way
to solve a problem.

583
00:45:04,403 --> 00:45:06,270
You have plenty of money, sir.

584
00:45:06,903 --> 00:45:09,824
Call it a settlement
or call it compensation.

585
00:45:10,071 --> 00:45:12,478
Five million dollars. Just five million.

586
00:45:12,537 --> 00:45:15,270
Pay that,
and we'll leave you alone for good.

587
00:45:19,815 --> 00:45:21,003
I'd rather not.

588
00:45:23,870 --> 00:45:24,903
Sir.

589
00:45:26,437 --> 00:45:29,270
I don't want to give people like you
a single cent.

590
00:45:33,370 --> 00:45:39,170
Get out. Get out now. Get out, you jerk.

591
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:44,303
I said get out, you jerk. Come here.

592
00:45:46,237 --> 00:45:48,537
How dare you...

593
00:45:48,570 --> 00:45:52,437
- Let go, you jerk!
- Who do you think I am?

594
00:45:54,523 --> 00:45:57,509
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

595
00:45:58,970 --> 00:46:02,470
This young lady is your twin sister?

596
00:46:03,270 --> 00:46:06,170
Yes, we're fraternal twins,
and my name is Han...

597
00:46:07,337 --> 00:46:11,203
Handpicked for style, Kim Gyu Min.

598
00:46:12,670 --> 00:46:14,703
I work part-time at a restaurant too.

599
00:46:14,937 --> 00:46:18,137
I wash my hands a lot,
so they dry out really fast.

600
00:46:19,003 --> 00:46:21,437
How can a student afford this?

601
00:46:21,503 --> 00:46:24,103
I told you, I have a part-time job too.
Please take it.

602
00:46:26,370 --> 00:46:29,119
- Thank you. I'll put it to good use.
- Okay.

603
00:46:29,839 --> 00:46:31,345
Not like that. Hurry and sit down.

604
00:46:31,370 --> 00:46:32,703
Sit down first, okay?

605
00:46:33,726 --> 00:46:37,832
I'm treating you two
to some delicious meat today.

606
00:46:37,857 --> 00:46:39,440
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

607
00:46:39,465 --> 00:46:41,153
Tap whatever you like here.

608
00:46:41,178 --> 00:46:44,100
You know how to tap,
right? Just touch here.

609
00:46:47,713 --> 00:46:51,024
Now I know what Gyu Seo meant.

610
00:46:52,456 --> 00:46:55,919
That you're warm.
It doesn't feel like we just met.

611
00:46:56,026 --> 00:46:58,775
It's like I've known you for a long time.

612
00:46:59,161 --> 00:47:00,486
That's a compliment, right?

613
00:47:00,527 --> 00:47:02,073
- Of course.
- Of course.

614
00:47:02,667 --> 00:47:05,360
Can I come visit often from now on?

615
00:47:05,598 --> 00:47:09,584
You're the ones who are busy.
I'd love that.

616
00:47:10,787 --> 00:47:14,028
- You don't have to be so formal with us.
- Little by little.

617
00:47:14,368 --> 00:47:18,101
Hurry and pick what you like,
and tap it right here like this.

618
00:47:18,135 --> 00:47:19,660
Go on, take a look.

619
00:47:20,252 --> 00:47:22,878
- Get something good.
- This looks delicious.

620
00:47:22,903 --> 00:47:24,899
(Daughter)

621
00:47:29,177 --> 00:47:30,433
Hey, Seo Hyeon.

622
00:47:30,458 --> 00:47:34,510
Dad got hurt, Mom.

623
00:47:34,665 --> 00:47:37,950
He got hurt? Where? How?

624
00:47:45,207 --> 00:47:46,460
Seo Hyeon.

625
00:47:49,394 --> 00:47:50,640
Where's Dad?

626
00:47:52,667 --> 00:47:54,251
You're here?

627
00:47:54,666 --> 00:47:58,846
It's nothing. Why did you call her?

628
00:47:58,954 --> 00:48:01,635
You dislocated your shoulder.
How is that nothing?

629
00:48:04,206 --> 00:48:07,259
It's really nothing.
I just stopped by the hospital for a bit.

630
00:48:07,406 --> 00:48:11,113
The doctors told you to stay,
but you insisted on coming home.

631
00:48:11,393 --> 00:48:12,935
I told you it's not like that.

632
00:48:12,960 --> 00:48:16,159
How did this even happen?

633
00:48:17,213 --> 00:48:20,943
I was practicing my golf swing.

634
00:48:21,077 --> 00:48:22,543
Golf, my foot...

635
00:48:22,545 --> 00:48:25,313
I heard a strange man came to your office.

636
00:48:25,800 --> 00:48:28,093
Where did you hear that?

637
00:48:28,193 --> 00:48:30,392
What strange man? He's a friend of mine.

638
00:48:30,754 --> 00:48:34,419
I have a friend who imports golf clubs,

639
00:48:34,444 --> 00:48:37,703
and he brought over a new model,
so I gave it a swing...

640
00:48:38,126 --> 00:48:42,053
What golf lesson ends up like this?

641
00:48:42,347 --> 00:48:44,653
I'm telling you, he got into a fight
with that strange man.

642
00:48:46,520 --> 00:48:49,573
When has he ever fought anyone?

643
00:48:49,753 --> 00:48:51,820
He wouldn't hurt a fly.

644
00:48:51,908 --> 00:48:53,451
Honestly, this kid.

645
00:48:53,480 --> 00:48:55,333
So that man hit you?

646
00:48:55,358 --> 00:48:57,637
What are you talking about?

647
00:48:57,707 --> 00:48:59,333
Stop making up boring stories.

648
00:49:01,107 --> 00:49:03,087
How did you get here when you're so busy?

649
00:49:03,780 --> 00:49:06,980
What kind of spouse wouldn't come?

650
00:49:10,306 --> 00:49:13,360
If I'd stayed at the hospital,
I wouldn't have to hear you nag.

651
00:49:13,385 --> 00:49:14,779
Honey, let's go inside.

652
00:49:50,006 --> 00:49:53,306
I'm fine. I think I just strained
a ligament or something.

653
00:49:53,486 --> 00:49:56,079
Remember last time I hurt my rib?
I'm fine.

654
00:50:02,153 --> 00:50:04,426
Who came to see you?

655
00:50:05,954 --> 00:50:08,530
- I told you, a friend.
- Which friend?

656
00:50:09,379 --> 00:50:10,926
Someone you don't know.

657
00:50:15,433 --> 00:50:17,399
Why do I feel so uneasy?

658
00:50:18,426 --> 00:50:22,190
Does someone have it in for you...

659
00:50:24,276 --> 00:50:28,610
No. You're not that kind of person.

660
00:50:30,491 --> 00:50:33,171
- Did you by any chance...
- By any chance what?

661
00:50:34,159 --> 00:50:36,837
Why are you making up stories too?

662
00:50:37,048 --> 00:50:38,593
I told you I'm fine.

663
00:50:40,972 --> 00:50:42,747
I'm fine. It's nothing.

664
00:50:46,873 --> 00:50:50,022
I'll get you a hot towel
for your hands and face.

665
00:50:58,989 --> 00:51:01,766
That Kang Sang Man, I swear.

666
00:51:03,853 --> 00:51:06,262
What if he tries to hurt Gyu Yeong?

667
00:51:07,465 --> 00:51:08,753
Now...

668
00:51:28,307 --> 00:51:30,085
Aren't you coming home?

669
00:51:31,099 --> 00:51:33,209
Are you gone for good?

670
00:51:36,813 --> 00:51:39,801
Are you getting a divorce? Because of me?

671
00:51:49,324 --> 00:51:53,840
Whatever happens from now on,
it won't be because of you.

672
00:51:55,172 --> 00:51:59,850
This is between your dad and me,
so leave it to us.

673
00:52:01,033 --> 00:52:03,996
So you're getting a divorce, anyway.

674
00:52:05,953 --> 00:52:09,192
I'll stay by your dad's side
until he gets better,

675
00:52:09,253 --> 00:52:10,976
so don't worry too much.

676
00:52:15,033 --> 00:52:16,882
Let me say it again.

677
00:52:16,912 --> 00:52:21,739
Whatever happens from now on,
it's not because of you, Seo Hyeon.

678
00:52:35,838 --> 00:52:38,605
(Jeong Woo)

679
00:52:40,373 --> 00:52:45,026
Unless it's serious,
don't call, text, or message me.

680
00:52:48,766 --> 00:52:50,469
Then who am I supposed to talk to?

681
00:52:50,766 --> 00:52:52,486
Who am I supposed to call?

682
00:52:53,069 --> 00:52:56,123
Where does "serious" start,
and where does it end?

683
00:52:57,546 --> 00:52:59,839
You've been my go-to person for venting
for almost 20 years,

684
00:52:59,864 --> 00:53:02,553
and now you draw a line overnight
and go on strike?

685
00:53:02,627 --> 00:53:04,660
No strike notice, no vote,

686
00:53:04,685 --> 00:53:07,517
you think I'll accept this illegal strike,
Park Jeong Woo?

687
00:54:06,439 --> 00:54:09,264
- Hey, Mu Jin.
- What are you doing?

688
00:54:10,074 --> 00:54:11,695
Getting ready to open the shop.

689
00:54:13,560 --> 00:54:15,421
I heard you went to see your mother today.

690
00:54:16,500 --> 00:54:19,127
- How did you know?
- Jeong Woo...

691
00:54:26,080 --> 00:54:27,386
Where are you?

692
00:54:27,546 --> 00:54:31,699
I'm on my way to a class reunion.

693
00:54:33,339 --> 00:54:35,392
Are you wondering how it went?

694
00:54:37,193 --> 00:54:39,181
I think it's going to take some time.

695
00:54:39,373 --> 00:54:42,247
Yeah, I figured it would.

696
00:54:42,827 --> 00:54:44,327
You'll wait for me, right?

697
00:54:44,800 --> 00:54:48,092
Of course.
I said I'd wait a hundred years.

698
00:54:49,546 --> 00:54:53,382
Okay. That makes me feel better.

699
00:54:54,183 --> 00:54:55,779
What a relief.

700
00:54:57,033 --> 00:55:00,273
Sorry for putting you through this.

701
00:55:01,379 --> 00:55:05,088
Okay. Make sure you eat dinner, Gyu Rim.

702
00:55:05,293 --> 00:55:07,466
You eat something good too, Mu Jin.

703
00:55:07,634 --> 00:55:10,887
- I love you.
- Me too.

704
00:55:11,767 --> 00:55:13,787
I love you too, Mu Jin.

705
00:55:42,700 --> 00:55:43,767
Gyu O.

706
00:55:43,865 --> 00:55:45,230
How's the opening prep going?

707
00:55:45,518 --> 00:55:46,963
Is there anything I can help with?

708
00:55:48,386 --> 00:55:50,067
No. I'm good.

709
00:55:51,685 --> 00:55:55,845
Here, this one's yours.
And this one's for Su Nam.

710
00:55:57,620 --> 00:55:59,826
Thanks. I'll enjoy it.

711
00:56:11,286 --> 00:56:13,067
Do you have something to tell me?

712
00:56:17,592 --> 00:56:18,669
What is it?

713
00:56:22,866 --> 00:56:25,302
I'm seeing Gyeol's teacher.

714
00:56:26,460 --> 00:56:27,880
What do you mean?

715
00:56:29,366 --> 00:56:33,378
Gyeol's teacher, Kwon Hui Na,
is my girlfriend.

716
00:56:35,986 --> 00:56:37,266
What are you talking about?

717
00:56:37,291 --> 00:56:38,871
What about Gyeol's teacher?

718
00:56:38,932 --> 00:56:41,200
How do you even know her?

719
00:56:45,753 --> 00:56:47,657
I first met her in high school,

720
00:56:48,115 --> 00:56:51,860
and after going around and around,
we finally got together today.

721
00:56:54,006 --> 00:56:58,846
I guess if two people are meant to be,
it happens one way or another.

722
00:57:01,546 --> 00:57:02,966
It'll be the same for you.

723
00:57:04,161 --> 00:57:08,303
Even if the whole world tries
to keep you and Mu Jin apart,

724
00:57:08,823 --> 00:57:10,525
you two are meant to be.

725
00:57:11,793 --> 00:57:13,600
You'll end up together in the end.

726
00:57:13,932 --> 00:57:16,759
I ran away as hard as I could too,
but I gave in today.

727
00:57:19,813 --> 00:57:21,826
I wanted you to be the first to know.

728
00:57:25,500 --> 00:57:27,729
Even if Gyeol's teacher is my girlfriend,
there won't be any special treatment.

729
00:57:27,761 --> 00:57:30,367
She never mixes work
and her personal life.

730
00:57:41,133 --> 00:57:43,647
I'm rooting for you, Han Gyu O.

731
00:57:46,040 --> 00:57:50,917
I'll always be on your side
and cheer you on.

732
00:57:57,010 --> 00:58:00,164
I knew you would.

733
00:58:01,800 --> 00:58:04,904
Then right back at you.

734
00:58:23,320 --> 00:58:26,279
But you'd better be careful too.

735
00:58:26,495 --> 00:58:30,640
That look.
That look gives me the wrong idea.

736
00:58:32,660 --> 00:58:35,465
That look, like you're under my spell.

737
00:58:37,266 --> 00:58:39,592
That look makes me wonder,
"Did she fall for me?"

738
00:58:39,972 --> 00:58:42,256
That look confuses me.

739
00:58:43,060 --> 00:58:44,490
When did I?

740
00:58:45,407 --> 00:58:48,795
When did I ever say
I was under your spell?

741
00:58:48,797 --> 00:58:51,226
When did I ever give you a look
that said I'd fallen for you?

742
00:58:51,699 --> 00:58:53,932
When did I ever confuse him?

743
00:58:54,527 --> 00:58:57,600
Should we just stop seeing each other?

744
00:58:57,625 --> 00:58:59,397
I don't have much life left,

745
00:59:00,136 --> 00:59:05,169
and I don't even have time to meet women,
let alone goof around with a friend.

746
00:59:06,730 --> 00:59:08,232
I don't need it.

747
00:59:09,159 --> 00:59:11,565
I don't need my son or a friend.
I don't need anyone.

748
00:59:13,046 --> 00:59:17,286
At this age, who needs a damn friendship
between a man and a woman?

749
00:59:21,513 --> 00:59:22,759
Come in.

750
00:59:24,014 --> 00:59:25,772
Are you heading home now?

751
00:59:27,574 --> 00:59:29,574
- Mom.
- What?

752
00:59:29,960 --> 00:59:34,073
Mu Jin's still in your office.

753
00:59:34,280 --> 00:59:36,110
Still on his knees.

754
00:59:37,180 --> 00:59:38,960
Has he lost his mind?

755
00:59:38,985 --> 00:59:41,398
You know you can't break his stubbornness.

756
00:59:43,127 --> 00:59:45,388
He'll die at this rate.

757
00:59:46,720 --> 00:59:49,707
If he's going to die like that,
then he'll die. What can I do?

758
00:59:50,861 --> 00:59:53,067
- Mom.
- Honestly.

759
00:59:53,260 --> 00:59:54,726
Foolish boy.

760
00:59:57,182 --> 01:00:00,482
(Namdong Hospital)

761
01:00:13,613 --> 01:00:15,504
You've already changed?

762
01:00:18,373 --> 01:00:19,879
Where do I go now?

763
01:00:19,904 --> 01:00:23,138
Just bite the bullet and go home.

764
01:00:23,193 --> 01:00:25,636
I told you I'd rather die than go there.

765
01:00:25,661 --> 01:00:27,473
Then where will you go?

766
01:00:27,673 --> 01:00:30,655
You can't go to a hotel
or your friend's place.

767
01:00:30,773 --> 01:00:34,539
How did you live your life
that you only have one friend?

768
01:00:37,126 --> 01:00:38,702
Should I just go to the Han River?

769
01:00:39,030 --> 01:00:41,236
Or defect to North Korea instead?

770
01:00:41,744 --> 01:00:43,427
You're driving me crazy, I swear.

771
01:00:43,467 --> 01:00:45,866
You said you'd protect me.

772
01:00:45,891 --> 01:00:48,070
One punch, six teeth, remember?

773
01:00:53,486 --> 01:00:58,298
What would happen
if your head and my fist...

774
01:00:58,323 --> 01:01:01,502
collided, just like that?

775
01:01:02,339 --> 01:01:05,006
What? I'd be out cold for sure.

776
01:01:05,031 --> 01:01:07,583
Right. That's it.

777
01:01:08,171 --> 01:01:10,895
- Then let's knock you out cold.
- What?

778
01:01:14,346 --> 01:01:17,133
What should I do with that wretched girl?

779
01:01:19,086 --> 01:01:22,519
I know a sly fox just like her myself.

780
01:01:24,740 --> 01:01:26,226
Heung Sik?

781
01:01:26,420 --> 01:01:28,339
I steamed the rice cakes you like,

782
01:01:28,364 --> 01:01:30,787
so hurry and come eat with me.

783
01:01:31,819 --> 01:01:36,206
That sly little vixen.

784
01:01:36,988 --> 01:01:38,670
What are you doing?

785
01:01:38,695 --> 01:01:40,870
I told you to hurry and come eat.

786
01:01:41,906 --> 01:01:45,012
What? Why'd you turn it off?
I was watching.

787
01:01:46,206 --> 01:01:48,498
Take this first.

788
01:01:48,993 --> 01:01:50,539
What's this?

789
01:01:51,873 --> 01:01:54,653
Why would I take a calming pill?

790
01:01:55,299 --> 01:02:00,172
Then try not to be too shocked,
and keep your wits about you.

791
01:02:00,259 --> 01:02:01,590
What are you talking about?

792
01:02:03,238 --> 01:02:04,781
What are you talking about?

793
01:02:04,806 --> 01:02:06,320
Bringing home a bride or something?

794
01:02:12,180 --> 01:02:14,202
Who's that?

795
01:02:15,367 --> 01:02:20,129
Why is the girl who supposedly got married
in my house this late at night?

796
01:02:20,154 --> 01:02:24,020
Well, Mom,
it's like something out of a drama...

797
01:02:24,120 --> 01:02:27,719
Drama or not, send her home right now.

798
01:02:27,744 --> 01:02:31,686
I felt so much better
when I didn't have to see that vixen.

799
01:02:31,884 --> 01:02:36,360
I thought I was seeing things tonight.

800
01:02:37,572 --> 01:02:39,232
Who's the vixen?

801
01:02:39,257 --> 01:02:40,894
Is she on TV?

802
01:02:41,379 --> 01:02:45,477
What? What's wrong with you?

803
01:02:46,227 --> 01:02:48,027
Well, Mom, the thing is...

804
01:02:48,272 --> 01:02:52,388
I don't like vixens. They scare me, lady.

805
01:02:52,413 --> 01:02:54,822
Hey, the calming pill.

806
01:02:54,912 --> 01:02:56,729
I told you to take it earlier.

807
01:02:56,754 --> 01:02:59,062
Heung Sik, get her out of here.

808
01:02:59,566 --> 01:03:01,894
Hurry, take it. Bottoms up.

809
01:03:06,253 --> 01:03:08,208
Get the vixen away from me.

810
01:03:08,233 --> 01:03:10,240
- I'm scared.
- I said get her out!

811
01:03:44,250 --> 01:03:47,127
Fine. You win.

812
01:03:52,039 --> 01:03:54,054
That's just the kind of guy you are.

813
01:03:55,892 --> 01:04:01,546
The more people try to stop you,
the more determined you get.

814
01:04:03,319 --> 01:04:07,199
Fine. You have my permission. Go ahead.

815
01:04:08,269 --> 01:04:13,808
Until you both get tired and sick of it,

816
01:04:14,288 --> 01:04:17,605
until you realize it and fall apart,

817
01:04:18,691 --> 01:04:24,366
go all the way and see it through.

818
01:05:17,169 --> 01:05:19,298
(Love on the Menu)

819
01:05:19,323 --> 01:05:21,929
Mud, gravel. None of it scares me.

820
01:05:21,954 --> 01:05:24,651
Will Han Gyu Rim feel the same way?
Want to bet?

821
01:05:24,676 --> 01:05:27,442
- Mom.
- Why couldn't you live a better life?

822
01:05:27,519 --> 01:05:30,138
Why couldn't you have lived any better?

823
01:05:30,139 --> 01:05:31,712
So you must have met Han Gyu Rim too?

824
01:05:31,737 --> 01:05:33,503
How long have you been lying to me?

825
01:05:33,528 --> 01:05:34,921
Mom? Who's my mom?

826
01:05:35,161 --> 01:05:36,706
How dare you call yourself that?

827
01:05:36,731 --> 01:05:38,353
Take it and get out right now!

828
01:05:38,378 --> 01:05:39,559
What do we do?

829
01:05:39,720 --> 01:05:42,400
All of our restaurant staff are gone.

830
01:05:42,553 --> 01:05:44,300
Are you really trying to leave Mu Jin
with nothing?

831
01:05:44,301 --> 01:05:46,079
Mu Jin still has plenty.

832
01:05:46,905 --> 01:05:48,705
Dramaday.me
